{"rev":13,"ts":"2026-10-29T22:04:23.164302349+00:00","fields":{"__previous_part_content__":"Previous Part: [05](05-lifecycle-handoff-and-reopen.md) | Next Part: [07](07-native-workflow-switch.md)\n\n# 06 — Discoverable named MCP surface\n\n## Outcome\n\nExpose the proposed granular Mission operations as discoverable named MCP tools\nwith capability/version metadata and one structured error envelope, replacing\nthe current generic-operation-only client experience.\n\n## Non-goal\n\nDo not retain a client obligation to run scripts for folder or waypoint\nlifecycle chores, and do not claim the surface is installed before W8.\n\n## Inputs and implementation boundary\n\nImplement exactly the proposal list and error codes in\n[ARTIFACTS.md](ARTIFACTS.md#settled-design-notes-proposals-not-current-apis)\nover W2-W5 service behavior. Generic compatibility may remain, but it is not\nthe required new-run path.\n\n## Expected post-state and validation\n\nMCP initialization/tool discovery returns each named operation, schemas require\nrevision/request-id where applicable, and representative success/error calls\nround-trip without client paths or shell scaffolding.\n\nFuture target: `cd workflow-tools && cargo test -p mission`; integration tests\nmust exercise initialize, tools-list, schemas, and structured error responses.\n\n## Checkpoint\n\nCommit MCP registration, schemas, and transport tests after passing.\n\n","__previous_part_id__":"213fa5ad-df2a-45a1-998d-cc5439ddb0b5","component":"mission.native-planning.named-mcp","depends_on":["9fcad997-7233-4305-9e69-534d4813ee2e"],"linked":["c616418e-8c27-4954-975e-490fc22c408f"],"parts":[{"id":"338e1b1c-256d-4303-90b2-b1964b7c8fac","kind":"requirements","path":"parts/requirements.md","frozen":false,"created_at":"2026-10-29T21:58:43.086826828Z"},{"id":"213fa5ad-df2a-45a1-998d-cc5439ddb0b5","kind":"design","path":"parts/design.md","frozen":false,"created_at":"2026-10-29T21:58:43.153936564Z"},{"id":"58547ded-b122-4146-af1f-906b4dd91a5f